<title>USA: Intl Specialty Products Inc Q1 net higher.</title>
<headline>Intl Specialty Products Inc Q1 net higher.</headline>
<dateline>WAYNE, N.J. 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Quarter</p>
<p>						    1997		 1996</p>
<p> Net sales				    $191.2	     $185.6</p>
<p>Costs and expenses:</p>
<p>    Cost of products sold		  114.2		112.9</p>
<p>    Selling, general and administrative 36.9		 35.2</p>
<p>    Goodwill amortization		    3.3		  3.3</p>
<p> Total costs and expenses		  154.4		151.4</p>
<p> Operating income			     36.8		 34.2</p>
<p> Interest expense			    (6.7)		(7.9)</p>
<p> Equity in earnings of joint venture     1.4		  1.4</p>
<p> Other income, net			     4.7		  3.6</p>
<p> Income before income taxes		 36.2		 31.3</p>
<p> Income taxes				 (13.0)	     (11.4)</p>
<p> Net income				     23.2		 19.9</p>
<p> Earnings per common share		  0.24		 0.20</p>
<p> Wgtd avg shrs (thousands)		96,474	     97,742</p>
<p> EBITDA(A)					56.0		 51.6</p>
<p>		   (Millions, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE A:  EBITDA represents earnings before income taxes,</p>
<p>increased by interest expense, depreciation and goodwill</p>
<p>amortization</p>
</text>
